WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.535
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back to the attic.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.103
I've been sittin' here
for about a half an hour,

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:06.105
waiting for my neighbor
to stop mowing his lawn,

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.274
but don't worry.
I've been passing the time

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:09.709
trying to remember
how much we paid

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:13.312
for the tiny chair behind me,
which, to my knowledge,

00:00:13.312 --> 00:00:15.048
neither of my children
ever, ever use.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.950
Because it turns out,
toddlers rarely say,

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.586
"I don't know about you, but,

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:21.154
I need to take a load off."

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.990
Maybe I can get the dog
to sit in it?

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.759
Maybe that would be cute
and I could Instagram it

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:28.061
or you could Instagram it.

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:30.029
Truth is,
I think the chair is useless.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:33.132
Speaking of useless,
that whole thing was a segue.

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:34.767
The Trump administration
understands

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.470
the importance of testing
to safely reopen the economy,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.871
because they're
testing themselves.

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:41.107
They just don't care
about testing you.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:42.909
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.712
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.014
Donald Trump doesn't just lie
about the big things.

00:00:49.014 --> 00:00:50.450
He also lies compulsively

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.985
about the smallest,
dumbest things,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.153
like how many people were
at his inauguration

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.489
or who drew a circle
on a hurricane map

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.425
or whether he's ever
even met Eric and Don Jr.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.127
"I'm sorry.
I'm not acquainted

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.429
with these two charming
business lizards."

00:01:03.429 --> 00:01:05.198
And the lies
about the small stuff

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.032
are red flags for the
lies about the big stuff.

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:09.268
For example, Trump visited
a Honeywell factory

00:01:09.268 --> 00:01:11.771
in Arizona Tuesday,
where they were making masks.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:14.640
You might remember the trip
from this indelible image

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.442
of Trump inspecting the masks

00:01:16.442 --> 00:01:19.179
while "Live and Let Die"
blasted in the background.

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.246
[ "Live and Let Die" plays ]
-The material

00:01:20.246 --> 00:01:22.649
that traps the particulates --

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:26.586
[ Drowning out speaker ]
-♪ Live and let die ♪

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.321
♪♪

00:01:29.321 --> 00:01:31.591
-My favorite part of that clip
is how oblivious Trump is

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.659
to what's going on around him.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:35.094
He's just nodding
and pointing at a mask

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:37.397
like a tourist
at a museum that's on fire.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:38.497
"They say she has that smile

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.700
because she likes
the smell of smoke."

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.802
But you might notice, based
on seeing his whole face,

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.338
that he is not, in fact,
wearing a mask

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.674
and, yet, when he spoke
to reporters on Wednesday,

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.943
he insisted he did,
in fact, wear a mask.

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:53.446
-Mr. President, yesterday,
you went to Arizona

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.947
and you had said,
before the trip,

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:57.516
that you would likely wear
a mask at the mask factory.

00:01:57.516 --> 00:01:58.751
You ended up not wearing one.

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:00.452
-Well, I actually did
have one, no.

00:02:00.452 --> 00:02:02.321
I put a mask on, yeah.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.856
I had a mask on
for a period of time.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:05.057
-We didn't see you
with a mask on.

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:06.859
-Well, I can't help it
if you didn't see me.

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:09.028
I mean, I had a mask on,
but I didn't need it.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.296
But I did put a mask on

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.932
and it was a Honeywell mask,
actually.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:16.869
And I also had a 3M mask and I
had about four other masks.

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:18.571
But I did have it on. I don't
know if you saw it or not,

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:21.006
but I had it on.
-How long did you have it
on for?

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:23.308
-Not too long, but I had it on.

00:02:23.308 --> 00:02:25.111
I had it on backstage.

00:02:25.111 --> 00:02:27.713
-Okay. First of all,
it's a factory.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.849
[ Laughing ]
There's not a backstage.

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.283
"Let's give those machines

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:33.386
everything they've
bargained for, boys!"

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:36.422
[ Laughing ] Also, to Trump,
everything's a beauty pageant.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.291
He was probably expecting the
machinists to be wearing sashes.

00:02:39.291 --> 00:02:41.193
"Hi, I'm Ted from Tucson
and, well,

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:43.129
I guess my talent is --
[ Mumbling ] I don't know.

00:02:43.129 --> 00:02:44.263
Makin' masks."

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.864
[ As Trump ] Very good, Ted.
Now, do a twirl.

00:02:45.864 --> 00:02:47.834
Okay. And, now,

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:50.069
can we see the swimsuit
portion of the factory?

00:02:50.069 --> 00:02:51.203
Is that nearby?

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:52.705
Second, what do you mean,

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:53.906
you can't help it
if we didn't see you?

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.741
We saw you.
You weren't wearing a mask.

00:02:55.741 --> 00:02:57.710
You were wearing goggles,
which is notable

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.013
because it's very weird to see
a renowned moron like Trump

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.680
wearing something
a scientist wears in a lab.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.317
It's like watching a dog
use a calculator.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.818
[ Thumping ]

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.887
[ As dog ]
[ Grumbles ]

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.055
Well, there's something
much more revealing

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:10.689
about this episode
than just the fact

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:12.592
that the president
is a compulsive liar.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:13.993
Trump didn't need to wear a mask

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.261
because he and all
the people around him

00:03:16.261 --> 00:03:17.797
have been tested
for coronavirus,

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:19.299
which is obviously
quite the luxury,

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:21.367
a luxury most Americans
don't have.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.236
White House Press Secretary
Kayleigh McEnany

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.604
was asked why
ordinary Americans

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.172
don't deserve the same
access to testing

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:29.041
that government officials
and corporate executives get

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:31.677
and she mocked the idea
of widespread testing as absurd.

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.446
-You said, at Honeywell,
that the president was told

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:34.914
by the folks at Honeywell,
as was the team,

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.215
that they didn't need
to wear masks.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.883
The reason he was told that
is because

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:39.418
the people who would be
interacting with him

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:41.954
had all been tested and had
been shown to be negative

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:43.722
before that took place,
I guess.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.491
So, the president
had those circumstances.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:48.394
Obviously, he's the president,
but why shouldn't all Americans

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:49.528
who go back to work

00:03:49.528 --> 00:03:51.230
be able to get a test
before they do it,

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.399
to feel comfortable
in their own work environment,

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:54.800
to be interacting
with other individuals?

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:58.737
-Yeah, well, let's dismiss
a myth about tests right now.

00:03:58.737 --> 00:04:00.839
If we tested every
single American

00:04:00.839 --> 00:04:02.741
in this country at this moment,

00:04:02.741 --> 00:04:04.444
we'd have to retest them
an hour later

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.178
and then an hour later
after that because,

00:04:06.178 --> 00:04:08.281
at any moment,
you could theoretically

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.082
contract this virus,
so the notion that

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:13.720
everyone needs to be tested
is just simply nonsensical.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:14.887
-Oh, good point.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.856
Maybe we should also stop
providing food, too,

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.025
because people will eat a meal
and then, four hours later,

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:20.859
they're just gonna
eat another meal.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.428
Or under quarantine
20 minutes later.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.829
But listen to what she's
saying there.

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:26.966
She's saying you don't need
to be tested to go back to work,

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.502
but the president and everyone
around him need to get tested

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.304
so he can go back to work safely

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:33.139
and freely engage
